Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that

$$
\begin{aligned}T(kv+hw)=T(kv)+T(hw)=kT(v)+hT(w)\end{aligned}
$$

for any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,

$$
\begin{aligned}T(2{v}_{1}+3{v}_{2}) & =2T({v}_{1})+3T({v}_{2}) \\ [\begin{aligned}7 \\ 4\end{aligned}] & =2T({v}_{1})+3[\begin{aligned}-1 \\ 2\end{aligned}] \\ 2T({v}_{1}) & =[\begin{aligned}7 \\ 4\end{aligned}]-3[\begin{aligned}-1 \\ 2\end{aligned}] \\ 2T({v}_{1}) & =[\begin{aligned}7 \\ 4\end{aligned}]-[\begin{aligned}-3 \\ 6\end{aligned}] \\ 2T({v}_{1}) & =[\begin{aligned}10 \\ -2\end{aligned}] \\ T({v}_{1}) & =\frac{1}{2}[\begin{aligned}10 \\ -2\end{aligned}] \\ T({v}_{1}) & =[\begin{aligned}5 \\ -1\end{aligned}].\end{aligned}
$$
